    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bbdb3645",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: this_chicken_is_so_rubbery; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts chef Gordon Ramsay looking displeased at a rubbery chicken dish, with text humorously suggesting that Goodyear (a tire company) called for the recipe because the chicken is so rubbery. The intent is to create humor through absurdity and wordplay, not to target any specific group. While the joke is about the texture of food, the implication that a rubbery chicken is so good it would be sought after by a tire company is a harmless, exaggerated analogy. The meme does not contain any abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic content. The humor is derived from the juxtaposition of a culinary critique with an unrelated corporate entity, which is a common comedic device. The overall intent is to entertain through absurd comparison, not to cause harm or promote harmful stereotypes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_b3ad62a5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
